# Expect Minecraft — Bedrock Behavior Pack

## Install
1. Zip this folder and rename to `.mcpack`, OR drag the `.mcpack` into
   Minecraft — the pack appears under **Behavior Packs** when editing a world.
2. Enable it. For older versions (< 1.21) you may also need to toggle
   **"Beta APIs"** under Experimental Features.
3. Add a `pack_icon.png` (128×128) if you want a custom icon in the UI.

## Commands
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `!help` | list all commands |
| `!spawn` | teleport to the world spawn |
| `!sethome` | save current position as home |
| `!home` | teleport to your saved home |
| `!heal` | restore health + hunger (admins) |
| `!gm <s\|c\|a\|sp>` | switch gamemode (admins) |
| `!stats` | show your stats |

## Making yourself admin
In-game, type: `/tag @s add admin`

## Compass shortcut
Right-clicking a compass teleports you to your saved home — a nice
HUD-free utility item driven entirely by script.

## Extending
- Add new commands to the `COMMANDS` object in `scripts/main.js`.
- Follow the pattern: `name(player, args) { ... }`.
- Persistent state uses `player.setDynamicProperty(key, value)`
  (strings/numbers/booleans only — serialize objects with `JSON.stringify`).
